What is 0.0872?  (0.03 / 0.0872 = 0.3440, the report's mapping constant)
================================================================================================
  0.03 / 0.3440                                    = 0.0872
  global std of latent                             = 0.2540   -> 0.03/x = 0.1181
  mean local std (W=9) of latent                   = 0.0943   -> 0.03/x = 0.3181
  median local std (W=9) of latent                 = 0.0872   -> 0.03/x = 0.3440
  mean local std (W=9) of in-focus blurred frame   = 0.0681   -> 0.03/x = 0.4404
  median local std of in-focus blurred frame       = 0.0642   -> 0.03/x = 0.4671
  mean local std (W=27) of latent                  = 0.1318   -> 0.03/x = 0.2277
  mean |grad| of latent                            = 0.0392   -> 0.03/x = 0.7660
  None of these is 0.0872 to better than ~10%; the constant is not reproducible
  from any committed artefact.

================================================================================================
Is the sigma -> sigma_rel mapping defensible IN PRINCIPLE?  Scale-invariance test.
================================================================================================
 plant amp    sigma |  gua/sel (est-sel)  median sigma_rel
       1.0   0.0300 |             0.9945            0.3707
       3.0   0.0900 |             0.9945            0.3707
       0.3   0.0090 |             0.9945            0.3707
  The whole forward model is linear and the estimator is scale-covariant, so a
  plant at amplitude a with noise a*sigma is identical to the unit plant at sigma.
  => sigma_local/signal_local IS the right invariant. The mapping is legitimate
     in kind; what remains is whether the CONSTANT is measured consistently.

